egui_stack continues egui_dock (https://github.com/anhosh/egui_dock, formerly
https://github.com/Adanos020/egui_dock), a docking system for egui released
under the MIT licence.

egui_dock was originally created by lain-dono and developed by Adam Gąsior
(Adanos020), later maintained by anhosh, with contributions from many people
whose names are kept in this repository's Git history.

egui_stack was forked from egui_dock's main branch after its 0.21.1 release
(tag egui_dock-0.21.1 in this repository). The move to egui 0.37 started from
an upstream pull request by crumblingstatue (egui_dock #354), its commits kept
with their author.

The sections module (src/sections) comes from egui-pop
(https://github.com/quazardous/egui-pop), released under MIT OR Apache-2.0
by the same maintainers and taken here under MIT.

The n-ary linear nodes of the tree (src/dock_state/tree), children with
shares in a row or a column, follow the model of egui_tiles
(https://github.com/rerun-io/egui_crates, crate egui_tiles), released under
MIT OR Apache-2.0 by Rerun Technologies AB. No code was copied from it.

The grid nodes of the tree (src/dock_state/tree/node/grid.rs) follow the
automatic grid of egui_tiles too: by default as many columns as the square
root of the number of children, rounded up. No code was copied from it.
